{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"agent_message","text":"I found a more direct authority question: `VerifyLeader` sets its threshold from the voter count, but registers confirmations with every replication peer, including nonvoters. The ordinary commitment and lease paths explicitly filter voters. I’ll prioritize whether nonvoter replies can complete verification; the storage-error lead remains open.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > build_backbone.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nm=json.load(open('../audit-spec/v1.json')); sources=[]; changes={}\ndef src(i,f,a,b,k='code_observation'):\n sources.append(dict(id=i,file=f,start_line=a,end_line=b,kind=k))\nfor args in [('M-elect-producer','raft.go',1976,2159),('M-install','raft.go',1814,1954),('M-user-restore','raft.go',1104,1200),('M-fsm','fsm.go',86,264),('M-fsm-contract','fsm.go',15,66,'interface_statement'),('M-membership','configuration.go',8,306),('M-membership-proposal','membership.md',1,36,'document_statement'),('M-api-apply','api.go',804,879,'interface_statement'),('M-api-verify','api.go',880,895,'interface_statement'),('M-future','future.go',13,133),('M-verify-vote','future.go',238,293),('M-verify-register','raft.go',965,989),('M-notify','replication.go',98,119),('M-heartbeat','replication.go',388,444),('M-lease','raft.go',1036,1097),('M-prevote','raft.go',1736,1813),('M-state','state.go',45,176),('M-snapshot','snapshot.go',125,277),('M-transfer','raft.go',990,1032),('M-timeout-now','raft.go',2209,2214),('M-net-heartbeat','net_transport.go',665,680),('M-trans-contract','transport.go',29,151,'interface_statement'),('M-error-test','raft_test.go',2744,2793,'test_expectation'),('M-error-store','log_cache_test.go',96,123),('M-dispatch-rpc','raft.go',1390,1439)]: src(*args)\nb={x['id']:x for x in m['behaviors']}\ndef upd(i,ss,**kw):\n b[i].update(kw);b[i]['source_ids']=list(dict.fromkeys(b[i]['source_ids']+ss));changes[i]=dict(impact='dependency',source_ids=ss,rationale='Read supporting producers, guards and completion paths; replace initial unread premise with conditional mechanism.',preserves='No accepted Candidate or Unit exists; existing quorum accounting meaning is unchanged.')\ndef add(i,a,o,c,t,ss,**kw):\n b[i]=dict(id=i,primary_activity=a,execution_owner=o,protocol_context=c,trigger=t,source_ids=ss,**kw)\nupd('B-vote',['M-elect-producer','M-prevote'],unknowns=['Split persistence of vote term and candidate requires separate failure-history investigation.'],important_branches=['electSelf persists new term then own vote; sends one RPC per other latest voter into a per-election buffered response channel','Pre-election does not persist or advance term; unsupported peer pre-vote counts as granted for compatibility','New vote persistence writes term first, then candidate; no grant on error. Duplicate same-term vote branch compares the stored candidate.'],consumes_fact_ids=['F-last-position'])\nupd('B-leader',['M-transfer','M-timeout-now','M-lease','M-elect-producer'],important_branches=['Election response channels are local to a campaign, so late replies cannot enter a subsequent campaign','Lease check counts only latest voters with recent contact and transitions to follower below quorum','Transfer waits for selected replica catch-up then sends TimeoutNow; target bypasses pre-vote and clears transfer privilege after candidate loop'],unknowns=['Detailed transfer cancellation and membership-overlap variants remain open.'])\nupd('B-apply-queue',['M-fsm','M-future','M-api-apply'],unknowns=[],external_effects=['Command/barrier and applicable configuration tuples queue to runFSM; lastApplied is queue progress, not a completed FSM call','runFSM invokes Apply or ApplyBatch, correlates responses by filtered input position, then responds to futures; barrier is not sent to user FSM','FSM loop may exit on shutdown; this map does not assert queued requests drain'],async_boundaries=['Single FSM goroutine serializes apply and restore; snapshots capture state there, persistence can run concurrently with later applies'])\nupd('B-reconstruct',['M-install','M-user-restore','M-state'],unknowns=[],produces_fact_ids=['F-last-position'],important_branches=['Restart reads actual LogStore.LastIndex and snapshot metadata, independent of old in-memory cache'])\nupd('B-append',['M-state'],produces_fact_ids=['F-last-position'],consumes_fact_ids=['F-last-position'],unknowns=['Whether normal leader retries can repair deleted suffix after one StoreLogs failure, before snapshot or restart; compare legal input history and storage test expectations.'])\nupd('B-replication',['M-heartbeat','M-trans-contract','M-net-heartbeat'],unknowns=['Pipeline error/response contract correspondence with concrete transport implementations remains unread.'],important_branches=['Snapshot fallback requires leader setupAppendEntries to encounter ErrLogNotFound, not merely follower rejection','Heartbeat requests carry no entries, previous entry or commit index; they can update contact without repairing missing history'])\nadd('B-membership','A4','Raft main goroutine','latest and committed configuration','serialized configuration request or received configuration entry',['M-membership','M-leader','M-dispatch','M-append'],implementation_guards=['Nonzero prevIndex must match latest index','Unique nonempty IDs/addresses and at least one voter','Admission waits for latest configuration commitment and current-term commit'],writes=['append new configuration, replace current commitment voter set, start/stop per-peer workers'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Voter eligibility determines commitment matches.','A2':'Latest voters determine election quorum and lease contact threshold.'},important_branches=['Current AddVoter directly makes a voter. membership.md is a proposal whose staging intent does not describe this current path.'])\nadd('B-snapshot','A3','snapshot worker plus main and FSM goroutines','snapshot index/term and configuration','local snapshot, InstallSnapshot or explicit user restore',['M-install','M-user-restore','M-snapshot','M-fsm'],writes=['snapshot position','applied position after restore','configuration on remote install','synthetic lastLog position on explicit user restore'],produces_fact_ids=['F-last-position'],implementation_guards=['Incoming snapshot rejects older terms; persists complete snapshot before waiting for FSM restore','Local snapshot cannot precede committed configuration index','User restore requires stable configuration and aborts inflight futures'],cross_activity_effects={'A2':'Remote install restores configuration and newer term; user restore retains current membership.','A1':'Leader snapshot response can contribute to its tenure commitment tracker.'},important_branches=['Remote install updates snapshot cache but not lastLog cache, then compacts or clears logs','User restore burns an index beyond current and imported positions to force snapshot transfer; public restore completion suffix not mapped'],unknowns=['Stale same-term snapshot and snapshot/log boundary variants remain open.'])\nadd('B-position','A6','raftState accessors under lastLock','one instance cached log and snapshot boundary','getLastIndex/getLastEntry',['M-state'],consumes_fact_ids=['F-last-position'],external_effects=['Returns max cached log/snapshot index; returns corresponding term, preferring log at equal index'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Append previous-entry fast path and follower commit bound trust this position.','A2':'Vote freshness and election requests trust this position.'})\nadd('B-client','A7','public API caller and Raft main loop','one apply/barrier future','ApplyLog or Barrier',['M-api-apply','M-future','M-leader'],implementation_guards=['Enqueue timeout only bounds admission; nonleader main loop rejects work'],external_effects=['Error completion precedes valid Index/Response reads; ErrLeadershipLost leaves outcome uncertain'],cross_activity_effects={'A5':'Successful Apply future exposes user FSM result after application.'})\nadd('B-verify-register','A2','Raft main goroutine','one verifyFuture in leader tenure and current membership','VerifyLeader future received with quorumSize zero',['M-api-verify','M-verify-register','M-leader','M-lease'],writes=['self vote = 1','quorumSize from latest voter count','future registered in each replState notification map'],produces_fact_ids=['F-verify-tally'],implementation_guards=['Single-voter quorum returns immediately','Leader exit responds ErrLeadershipLost'],unknowns=['No registration filter for nonvoters is visible, unlike lease counting.'])\nadd('B-verify-confirm','A2','replication and heartbeat workers plus verifyFuture voteLock','registered peer callbacks for a future','successful append/snapshot, heartbeat response or stale-term rejection',['M-notify','M-heartbeat','M-match','M-replicate','M-verify-vote'],consumes_fact_ids=['F-verify-tally'],produces_fact_ids=['F-verify-tally'],writes=['detach pending future map per peer then vote(bool)','increment votes on true; notify at threshold; false notifies immediately'],implementation_guards=['Cleared peer map prevents repeat callback for that registration','notifyCh nil prevents further processing after notification'],important_branches=['vote receives only a boolean, not peer identity or suffrage'],unknowns=['Can reachable nonvoters supply the missing confirmations while other voters supply none?'])\nadd('B-verify-result','A2','Raft main goroutine','notified verifyFuture','verifyCh receives existing future',['M-consume','M-verify-vote','M-api-verify'],consumes_fact_ids=['F-verify-tally'],external_effects=['Below threshold steps down and responds ErrNotLeader; threshold responds nil','Removes pending notifications from replication states'],cross_activity_effects={'A7':'Public VerifyLeader is documented for preventing stale FSM reads after lost leadership.'})\nm['behaviors']=list(b.values())\nm['facts'] += [dict(id='F-last-position',meaning='Cached log and snapshot index/term pairs used to represent this instance latest retained history position; updates occur on successful append, restart or snapshot paths. Failed append after truncation can leave older cache values.',identity={'owner':'Raft instance','position':'lastLogIndex/Term and lastSnapshotIndex/Term'},validity_context='Accessor locks provide coherent pairs, not proof that cached log is still present after storage failure; user restore intentionally synthesizes a log boundary backed by snapshot.',representation=['raftState lastLogIndex,lastLogTerm,lastSnapshotIndex,lastSnapshotTerm'],durability='Volatile metadata referring to caller stores.',recovery='NewRaft rebuilds from actual store and snapshot; remote install changes snapshot boundary.',source_ids=['M-state','M-append','M-start','M-install','M-user-restore']),dict(id='F-verify-tally',meaning='A verifyFuture starts with one self vote and increments for positive callbacks from registered replication workers; its completion threshold is derived from voter count. The tally itself carries no voter identities.',identity={'owner':'verifyFuture instance','context':'leader tenure registration'},validity_context='Pending verification; peer notification maps detach callbacks and voteLock/notifyCh limit completion notification. Callback suffrage eligibility has not been established.',representation=['verifyFuture.votes','verifyFuture.quorumSize','verifyFuture.notifyCh','followerReplication.notify'],durability='Volatile; not persisted.',recovery='New request and leader tenure establish new registration; leader exit responds leadership loss.',source_ids=['M-verify-register','M-verify-vote','M-notify','M-leader'],invalidators=['B-leader'])]\nm['surfaces'][1].update(disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['B-snapshot'],reason='Snapshot installation and user restoration traced; boundary variants remain open.',source_ids=['M-install','M-user-restore','M-snapshot'])\nm['surfaces'] += [dict(entry_point='Raft.persistVote partial storage failure',disposition='deferred',reason='Vote term and candidate persist separately; investigate prior candidate plus failed candidate write before alleging duplicate-vote failure.',source_ids=['M-elect-producer','M-vote'],high_consequence=True),dict(entry_point='Raft.verifyLeader peer eligibility',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['B-verify-register','B-verify-confirm','B-verify-result'],reason='Voter-derived threshold with registration over all replication peers is selected for investigation.',source_ids=['M-verify-register','M-verify-vote','M-membership'],high_consequence=True)]\nfor a in m['activities']:\n a['source_ids']=sorted(set(s for x in b.values() if x['primary_activity']==a['class_id'] for s in x['source_ids']))\n a.pop('behavior_ids',None)\n a['realization_summary']={'A1':'Term-bound majority match tracking advances leader commitment; follower append validates/stores history and advances from leader commit.','A2':'Per-election voter requests acquire authority; higher terms, lease loss and transfer change context. VerifyLeader counts peer callbacks against a voter-derived threshold, with eligibility unresolved.','A3':'Ordinary/pipeline replication retry and snapshot fallback resynchronize peers; explicit user restore has distinct semantics.','A4':'Latest membership controls eligibility, with serialized changes and at least one unique voter; current AddVoter directly grants voter status.','A5':'Committed tuples queue to one FSM worker; response occurs after application while lastApplied tracks queue progress.','A6':'Storage and snapshot reconstruction supply cached history positions used by append and voting.','A7':'API futures distinguish admission, application and leadership-loss uncertainty; caller FSM and transport/storage implementations have separate duties.'}[a['class_id']]\nov=m['core_overview'];ov['status']='usable';ov['core_gaps']=[]\nov['formation']['explanation']='Leader persists assigned term/index entries then records its match. Per-peer workers accept successful append/snapshot responses into a tenure-specific voter tracker; newer terms signal loss of authority. Majority index must reach the current-term startIndex. Main loop consumes commit notification, advances configuration and queues ordered command/barrier tuples to one FSM worker; successful application futures complete after Apply/ApplyBatch. Followers validate previous term, reconcile/store suffix and consume propagated leader commit. Periodic ordinary replication propagates commitment; empty fast-path heartbeats do not. Failed pipeline returns to ordinary retries, whose missing leader logs cause snapshot fallback.'\nov['formation']['source_ids']+=['M-fsm','M-heartbeat'];ov['formation']['behavior_ids']+=['B-snapshot']\nov['context']['explanation']='Heartbeat expiry permits configured voters to campaign. Pre-vote does not advance term; actual election persists term and self-vote, asks each other latest voter once and tallies a per-campaign channel. Vote handlers reject ineligible candidates and stale histories, and persist a new vote before granting. Newer terms, voter lease loss or removal cause authority loss; tenure exit resolves pending leader futures and stops workers. Transfer waits for selected replication catch-up then TimeoutNow triggers a privileged election. Snapshot installation and restart reconstruct history/configuration; explicit user restore aborts pending writes and creates a new snapshot-backed boundary.'\nov['context']['source_ids']+=['M-elect-producer','M-lease','M-transfer','M-install','M-user-restore'];ov['context']['behavior_ids']+=['B-snapshot','B-membership']\nov['connection']['explanation']='Voting log freshness links future authority to retained history; new tenure commitment starts empty and requires a current-term entry before inherited prefix can commit. Old replication workers retain old tracker and stepDown channels; old election replies retain old campaign channels. Latest voter membership controls election and commitment, changes are gated by prior configuration/current-term commitment, and suffix truncation can revert pending membership. Snapshot metadata records committed membership and restore/restart rebuild context. Client leader loss is uncertain completion, distinct from completed FSM application. Verification is another authority consumer: its voter-count threshold is fed by all registered peer callbacks, an unresolved eligibility discrepancy.'\nov['connection']['source_ids']+=['M-elect-producer','M-membership','M-api-apply','M-verify-register','M-verify-vote'];ov['connection']['behavior_ids']+=['B-membership','B-verify-register','B-verify-confirm']\nov['open_details']=['VerifyLeader nonvoter callback eligibility is the principal selected discriminator.','Transient failed append after successful truncation: recovery before restart/snapshot remains unresolved; existing injected-error test covers nonconflicting appends.','Split vote persistence failure history and old snapshot boundary behavior remain sourced open surfaces.','Transport pipeline error correspondence and deeper transfer overlap paths remain unread.']\nov['rationale']='Representative formation and authority paths and their history, membership, recovery and completion dependencies are now traced; local discrepancies remain explicit without presumed violations.'\nfor key in ['core_overview','activities','surfaces']:\n changes[key]=dict(impact='dependency',source_ids=['M-elect-producer','M-fsm','M-install','M-user-restore','M-membership','M-verify-register'],rationale='Complete backbone and retain newly sourced unresolved surfaces.',preserves='No accepted Candidate or Unit exists; prior partial conclusions remain scoped.')\n# Drop controller reverse indexes, which are regenerated.\nfor f in m['facts']:\n f.pop('established_by',None);f.pop('consumed_by',None)\njson.dump(m,open('backbone-map.json','w'),indent=2)\nq=dict(question='Can VerifyLeader complete successfully using nonvoter confirmations when the leader has no confirmation from another voter, despite its threshold being derived from the voter set?',importance='False authority verification could permit callers to serve stale FSM reads after a voter majority has moved to a new leader. A local eligibility discrepancy is distinct from proving an end-to-end stale read.',source_ids=['M-api-verify','M-verify-register','M-verify-vote','M-notify','M-membership','M-lease','M-leader'],participants=['leader','other voters','nonvoter replication peer'],objects=['verifyFuture','followerReplication.notify'],contexts=['fixed configuration with three voters and at least one nonvoter','one pending verification in leader tenure'],event_paths=['VerifyLeader -> leaderLoop -> verifyLeader -> peer notifyAll -> verifyFuture.vote -> leaderLoop response'],activity_classes=['A2'],behavior_ids=['B-verify-register','B-verify-confirm','B-verify-result'],fact_ids=['F-verify-tally'],supporting_behavior_ids={'B-membership':'Defines voter versus nonvoter eligibility and stable configuration.','B-leader':'Creates replication state for each configured peer and supplies separate lease/exit protection.'},obligation_relation_kind='consumption',counterevidence=['Lease check filters voters and may independently step down later; the schedule must not assume it is absent forever.','Leader exit aborts verification, and false callback can force rejection.','A local success would not alone demonstrate stale application data or a second leader.'],unknowns=['Does full public verification complete from nonvoter support under a legal bounded schedule before lease loss?','What precise responsibility applies to verification support membership independently of whole-cluster stale-read consequence?'],disposition='concrete_suspicion',preferred_check='controlled_schedule',priority=3,trigger_rationale='Commitment and lease explicitly filter voters; verification registers all replState peers and passes only booleans to the tally. A small constructor-based check can distinguish real callback eligibility from an unseen alternate guard. This is more direct authority-safety work than the storage-error recovery lead, whose failure applicability and indefinite recovery remain less settled.')\ns=dict(action='continue',rationale='Complete the two-line backbone and select the newly sourced verification eligibility discrepancy; retain storage-error and split-vote-persistence leads without findings.',sources=sources,map_path='backbone-map.json',map_changes=changes,question=q,feedback=dict(ref_ids=['M-error-test','M-error-store','M-replicate','M-install','M-verify-register','M-verify-vote'],answered='An existing test expects further commands to apply after injected follower StoreLogs failure, but it does not create a conflicting suffix. Snapshot fallback is conditional on missing leader logs, not follower failure alone. Separately, verification uses a voter-derived threshold with registration across all replication peers; this supplies a more direct authority discriminator.',remaining=['Construct a legal verification history preserving leader lease timing, callback ownership and fixed voter/nonvoter membership.','Retain the truncation lead for source/conditional exploration; no permanent failure or safety outcome established.'],understanding='updated',rationale='Source reading completes the backbone and justifies choosing the direct authority question over more conditional recovery work.'))\njson.dump(s,open('submission-next.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python build_backbone.py\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-06_11-00-45-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission submission-next.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
